From: Adarsh Jagadish Kamini <adarsh.jagadish.kamini@est.tech>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: do not add ${prefix}/include when cross compiling

Since 3.0, configure adds -I${prefix}/include to CPPFLAGS while it
checks for declarations in elf.h and dwarf.h. When cross compiling,
${prefix}/include is /usr/include on the build host, and the compiler
rejects it with -Wpoison-system-directories.

The headers are found through the sysroot in that case, so only add
the prefixed include dir for native builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Adarsh Jagadish Kamini <adarsh.jagadish.kamini@est.tech>
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1202,7 +1202,7 @@
 AM_CONDITIONAL([ENABLE_LIBABIGAIL_MULTITHREADING],[test "x$ENABLE_MULTITHREADING" = "xyes"])
 
 use_prefixed_includedir=""
-if test x$prefix != x; then
+if test x$prefix != x && test x$cross_compiling != xyes; then
   use_prefixed_includedir=$prefix
 fi
 
